    {
      "path": "/usr/local/var/cyclotron/tmp.noindex/cyclotron-e78afdd4/samples/eef94c798fdb/2026-10-25_d5c2804f94671eaba2aed99a7c4f93ac_coinminer_ezcob_glassworm_poet-rat_sliver_snatch",
      "sha256": "eef94c798fdb20435e3cfd55d5689cf9a6af7e3586ac4762b431e86998ef8757",
      "verdict": "MALICIOUS",
      "marker_line": "Go infector + GravityRAT: overwrites files; add path-report detection",
      "evidence": [
        "Recovered Go pclntab at raw offset 0x3f5920. Native disassembly resolves main.main at 0x62d190, main.visit at 0x62c450, main.plant_start_up at 0x62cba0 and main.add_startup at 0x62cae0.",
        "main walks C:\\Program Files\\. The callback reads each matching non-directory, obtains mutated self bytes, overwrites the visited path with ioutil.WriteFile, and writes another generation-marked executable. This replaces unrelated files, rather than updating an owned component.",
        "plant_start_up constructs random .exe names under C:\\Windows\\System32\\, writes mutated copies and calls add_startup. add_startup opens the HKLM CurrentVersion\\Run key and writes the copied executable path. Actual filesystem/registry permission success is unknown; no privilege-escalation behavior is claimed.",
        "main formats generation/lineage, a self-image hash, PRNG seed and its os.getModuleFileName execution path into an HTTPS query and passes the URL to net/http.Client.Get. A second GET targets a randomized RequestBin hostname. The new hostile profile requires an actual infector, HTTP GET reference and a self-hash/execution-path query template; it does not require either observed domain.",
        "get_self_mutated_bytes Base64-decodes the 0xd705c-byte constant at raw offset 0x2ca606 and appends the decoded image plus padding. Decoding recovers a 660480-byte LSASS 1.9.1201.10 image and a 69-byte footer. SHA256 of the PE is 1c0ea462f0bbd7acfdf4c6daf3cb8ce09e1375b766fbd3ff89f40c0aa3f4fc96, listed as GX in Talos. No inspected native path transfers execution into the appended managed payload.",
        "CIL Program.Main -> Initialize -> Services.Start -> DomainController.Start -> RootJob and TaskJobs. A five-minute timer polls for tasks. The task switch supplies task Args to CmdManager; cmd.exe /c redirects command output into a file, and UploadManager sends that path with WebClient.UploadFileTaskAsync.",
        "FileHelper filters recursive drive enumeration for document extensions. ScanManager sends the inventory and UploadManager sends selected files. UsbManager watches logical-disk arrival, copies filtered files to staging, and uploads them on a ten-minute timer. ProcessManager, PortManager and ServicesManager separately generate and upload process, netstat -a and installed-service reports. Identity/domain and VM notes are sent to the GX endpoint. Existing eight hostile and three suspicious managed-module findings remain supported.",
        "The scanner labels several extracted LSASS analysis units Mono.Cecil.dll because a resource name occurs inside them. That extraction label is not the identity of the module. YARA predicates bind the RAT signatures to each current image CLR heaps; the genuine Mono.Cecil resource units have zero hostile findings. Repeated overlapping/appended images are not separate malware families.",
        "The native unwanted rewriting independently establishes MALICIOUS. Deployment details and runtime success are not supplied. The sandbox score and collector filename were not used as proof."
      ],
